     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Meena heard her father mention paying tax. \"Why do we pay tax?\" she asked."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "revenue",
     "direct tax",
     "indirect tax",
     "GST",
     "budget",
     "deficit"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "A government earns revenue and spends it on public services. Its revenue comes from taxes and non-tax sources such as fees and profits from public enterprises. Taxes are direct, like income tax paid by the person, and indirect, like GST added to prices.\nGoods and Services Tax (GST) replaced many indirect taxes in 2017. The budget is the yearly statement of the government's income and expenditure. A deficit occurs when spending is more than income.\nTax money builds roads, schools, hospitals and defence, and funds welfare schemes. Paying tax honestly is a duty of citizens."
    }
